{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1174467-purified-martial-arts","id":1174467,"title":"Purified Martial Arts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-08T22:21:26-08:00","id":1174467,"title":"Purified Martial Arts","content":"So this is less a full fledged idea and more a random musing at 1 AM but it's a musing that entertains me. If you take a couple Purified, give them a secure Essence supply, time and an interest in martial arts then you potentially have the seeds for something awesome. There are various concepts in some arts that can't be trained effectively because if (please note the if) they work as advertised then you may be down a training partner. The problem is that the less thoroughly you train a technique, the less guarantee that it will work as advertised. This leaves humans with a problem that generally leads to a focus on things that can b trained to a reliable standard. Purified with a steady supply of Essence however aren't nearly as worried. Their anatomy is still basically human but the body is easily repaired even from catastrophic damage. Long as you can find a couple Purified willing to train together, you have a perfect explanation for people roaming around who know how to reliably stop a heart with one blow or other insane stunts because Purified can actually train those techniques full bore against each other. If someone's heart stops, who cares? They'll be up again in a few minutes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11422-maskedone","name":"MaskedOne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T23:13:05-08:00","id":1174474,"title":"","content":"True. You can also get the same results by getting a lot of expendable sparring partners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T09:51:11-08:00","id":1174893,"title":"","content":"This is one of the reasons I allow certain supernatural characters to have quite a few dots in combat skills already at character generation. There are plenty of splats that can heal damage, so then they can try out more devastating techniques, be wounded and crippled and then be up for the next round less than an hour later. In one Werewolf game I let the players know that if their characters wanted they could begin the game with lots of brutal sparring and exercises behind them (and many dots in combat skills and merits) simply as a logical consequence of their amazing ability to regenerate damage.<br /> <br /> Certain mages (or orders of mages) I imagine could even make expendable targets to practice on, such as golems, homunculi or even summoned spirits. Just expect Wisdom losses for handling the two latter this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T12:05:14-08:00","id":1176814,"title":"","content":"Mechanically, I could see this done as either a Style Merit which has a more mundane martial arts Style Merit at 5 dots and a high level in whatever applicable Skill as prerequisites, or possibly as a set of 'techniques', each formalized as a 1-3 dot Merit, with similar prerequisites.<br /> <br /> In story terms, though, I really like this. I'm a massive fan of magic martial arts, and an even greater one of mundane-but-it-looks-magic martial arts. Plus the Purified fit the 'ancient martial arts hermit in a mountain temple' to a tee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T18:21:07-08:00","id":1177112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1174467-purified-martial-arts?p=1174474#post1174474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. You can also get the same results by getting a lot of expendable sparring partners.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's potentially a lot of sparring partners. It's doable depending on the place and time period but if you're using humans then you're gonna draw a decent amount of attention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1174467-purified-martial-arts?p=1174893#post1174893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of the reasons I allow certain supernatural characters to have quite a few dots in combat skills already at character generation. There are plenty of splats that can heal damage, so then they can try out more devastating techniques, be wounded and crippled and then be up for the next round less than an hour later. In one Werewolf game I let the players know that if their characters wanted they could begin the game with lots of brutal sparring and exercises behind them (and many dots in combat skills and merits) simply as a logical consequence of their amazing ability to regenerate damage.<br /> <br /> Certain mages (or orders of mages) I imagine could even make expendable targets to practice on, such as golems, homunculi or even summoned spirits. Just expect Wisdom losses for handling the two latter this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that I'd give out free dots too much for it simply because not everyone who can actually take the type of full on sparring will be interested in doing so anymore then everyone who can learn to write a program actually develops skill in it. If I were to mechanize this concept then it'd probably be represented in merits of some kind. That said, weres and some mages would certainly have options to exploit this type of training.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1174467-purified-martial-arts?p=1176814#post1176814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically, I could see this done as either a Style Merit which has a more mundane martial arts Style Merit at 5 dots and a high level in whatever applicable Skill as prerequisites, or possibly as a set of 'techniques', each formalized as a 1-3 dot Merit, with similar prerequisites.<br /> <br /> In story terms, though, I really like this. I'm a massive fan of magic martial arts, and an even greater one of mundane-but-it-looks-magic martial arts. Plus the Purified fit the 'ancient martial arts hermit in a mountain temple' to a tee.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm something of a fan of skills so advanced that they look like magic to anyone who doesn't have a high degree of understanding. That or for story purposes, skills that are so advanced that they may actually cross the line ever so slightly into supernatural but you can't prove it without extremely close inspection. If an onlooker can look at something and walk away with the question of, &quot;Was that actually magic or not?&quot; then I consider it a plus. I think it's especially appropriate for Purified who are probably better off not trying to match raw power with anyone but get a <i>a lot</i> of skill dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11422-maskedone","name":"MaskedOne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T05:42:02-08:00","id":1182882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MaskedOne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1174467-purified-martial-arts?p=1177112#post1177112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that I'd give out free dots too much for it simply because not everyone who can actually take the type of full on sparring will be interested in doing so anymore then everyone who can learn to write a program actually develops skill in it. If I were to mechanize this concept then it'd probably be represented in merits of some kind. That said, weres and some mages would certainly have options to exploit this type of training.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said nothing about free dots. I simply allow some supernatural characters to put more than 3 of their starting skill dots in a skill (not just fighting skills) if they can describe how they have used their supernatural abilities to hone their skills more than a normal person could. A werewolf for example has been able to train more intensely to fight because of their regeneration but of course not all werewolves will have the iron discipline or passion to maintain such a training regime. As another example, a Mage with high dots in Mind magic could reasonably be allowed to put a lot of their starting skill dots in a social skill because they have gained a lot of intuitive understanding of people from all the readings of auras and thoughts.<br /> <br /> Of course, focussing so much into one single skill leaves the other skills weak, which I occasionally exploit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T13:09:35-08:00","id":1183028,"title":"","content":"You do know that anyone's allowed to buy up to five dots of any skill without any special permission?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T05:54:00-08:00","id":1183231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1174467-purified-martial-arts?p=1183028#post1183028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do know that anyone's allowed to buy up to five dots of any skill without any special permission?</div> </div> </div> </div>3 dots is usually pointed out as a max amount for starting characters if I'm not mistaken. And even if I'm mistaken I really would not allow just any character to buy more than 3 without a good reason for doing so.<br /> <br /> But that's just my style since I like my games very down to earth. If I want superhero characters I do not GM Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 02-07-2018, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T11:31:51-08:00","id":1183325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1174467-purified-martial-arts?p=1183231#post1183231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3 dots is usually pointed out as a max amount for starting characters if I'm not mistaken. And even if I'm mistaken I really would not allow just any character to buy more than 3 without a good reason for doing so.<br /> <br /> But that's just my style since I like my games very down to earth. If I want superhero characters I do not GM Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are mistaken? The original pointed out how you need two points to get the fifth dot, and the GMC update just removed that limitation. I don't remember anything putting a cap on it, and those statements would suggest that you are quite capable of putting five dots into something at the very start.<br /> <br /> Not that it is a bad house rule. It does help with the lower-power feel you are going for, and might prevent minmaxing and allow for more well-rounded characters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T16:15:04-08:00","id":1183415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1174467-purified-martial-arts?p=1183231#post1183231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really would not allow just any character to buy more than 3 without a good reason for doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I need you to shout this in my ear the next time that one player tries to start with five dots of Melee (Greatsword). Yes this was in a modern game. No he didn't have a reason better than &quot;so I can one-shot werewolves&quot;. Long story.<br /> <br /> I too dimly recall three dots being given as a good maximum for starting skills somewhere, but Ruger is right that it was never an actual rule in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T01:36:03-08:00","id":1183510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1174467-purified-martial-arts?p=1183415#post1183415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I too dimly recall three dots being given as a good maximum for starting skills somewhere, but Ruger is right that it was never an actual rule in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in at least some WoD lines. I remember it from Kindred of the East.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T07:26:25-08:00","id":1183579,"title":"","content":"It was a rule in oWoD, and even then not quite - you were limited to three dots when allocating your base allotment of Skills, but could raise them further with Bonus Points.<br /> <br /> Then, in nWoD 1e, you could allocate your dots however you wanted, but the fifth dot in anything cost you two dots.<br /> <br /> Then, in nWoD 2e a.k.a. Chronicles of Darkness, even that limitation is gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}